00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.840
For those of you who have not
attended a previous session,

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.780
just a quick highlight, a
Kubernetes-based building

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.610
blocks for serverless workloads.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:14.390
So one of the key drivers
or key properties of Knative

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.740
is that it sets some key
primitives for building

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.120
applications on top of Knative.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.530
It provides initially build,
eventing, and serving.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.650
And those are very first efforts
to simplify that experience,

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.270
and we're going to go after
other areas pretty soon, too.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.100
It solves many of the
modern development patterns.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.820
What I mean by modern here
is that, if you are bringing

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:41.030
a database, a single-node
database, probably

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.710
not the greatest place to run
this on top of Knative today.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:45.950
But if you're looking
for a microservice

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.320
to build microservices,
stateless microservice

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.020
or Twelve-Factor
applications, Knative really

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.630
solves a lot of big
problems or issues related

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.160
to deploying on
top of Kubernetes,

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.762
those type of workloads.

00:03:57.762 --> 00:03:59.720
Knative also implements
a lot of good learnings

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:06.470
from Google, including 10 plus
years on op engine, Kubernetes,

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.650
and Istio itself from the
open source community,

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.340
as well as a number of
contributions and feedback

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.600
and inputs from our partners.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:21.950
So these are the companies, like
Red Hat, IBM, Pivotal, and SAP,

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.500
that have worked with us
before we even opened the repo,

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.072
over the last six months or so.

00:04:26.072 --> 00:04:27.530
We really could
not have been where

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.420
we are today without them.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.730
In addition to
that, we also have

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.990
started collaborating very early
with a number of open source

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.660
frameworks out there,
function as a service

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.470
frameworks, that are kind of
building on top of Kubernetes.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.180
And the signal
that was coming out

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.610
of that that was really
good is that many of them

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.760
already are either taking
Knative as an ingredient

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.860
into their stack
or replatforming

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:55.370
the entire framework
on top of Knative

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.980
to simplify a lot of
the boring tasks that

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.670
are related to running your
framework on top of Kubernetes.

